般的です。","related_terms":["die Sitzung","der Termin"],"source_note":"J-Connect original example and explanation","source_refs":["j-connect-editorial"],"quality_tier":"editorial-reviewed","verification_status":"j-connect-editorial-reviewed","updated_at":"2026-08-14","verified_at":"2026-08-14"},{"card_id":"a2-001","lemma":"unterwegs","display_de":"unterwegs","unit_type":"word","part_of_speech":"adverb","primary_level":"A2","level_tags":["A2"],"topic_tags":["daily","日常","work","仕事"],"scene_tags":["daily","work"],"japanese":"移動中で、出先で","example_de":"Ich bin noch unterwegs und komme zehn Minuten später.","example_ja":"まだ移動中で、10分遅れて着きます。","grammar":{"usage":"場所・状態を表す副詞。sein と組み合わせる。"},"collocations":["noch unterwegs sein","unterwegs anrufen"],"learning_note":"移動中であることを簡潔に伝える便利な表現です。","related_terms":["ankommen","sich verspäten"],"source_note":"J-Connect original example and explanation","source_refs":["j-connect-editorial"],"quality_tier":"editorial-reviewed","verification_status":"j-connect-editorial-reviewed","updated_at":"2026-08-14","verified_at":"2026-08-14"},{"card_id":"a2-002","lemma":"sich beeilen","display_de":"sich beeilen","unit_type":"phrase","part_of_speech":"verb","primary_level":"A2","level_tags":["A2"],"topic_tags":["daily","日常"],"scene_tags":["daily"],"japanese":"急ぐ","example_de":"Wir müssen uns beeilen, sonst verpassen wir den Bus.","example_ja":"急がないとバスに乗り遅れます。","grammar":{"third_person":"beeilt sich","past_participle":"beeilt","auxiliary":"haben","separable":false,"reflexive":true,"government":"sich (Akkusativ) beeilen"},"collocations":["sich ein bisschen beeilen","Bitte beeilen Sie sich."],"learning_note":"再帰代名詞を忘れないでください。命令形でも Beeilen Sie sich! です。","related_terms":["eilig","zu spät"],"source_note":"J-Connect original example and explanation","source_refs":["j-connect-editorial"],"quality_tier":"editorial-reviewed","verification_status":"j-connect-editorial-reviewed","updated_at":"2026-08-14","verified_at":"2026-08-14"},{"card_id":"a2-006","lemma":"ausfallen","display_de":"ausfallen","unit_type":"word","part_of_speech":"verb","primary_level":"A2","level_tags":["A2"],"topic_tags":["daily","日常","work","仕事"],"scene_tags":["daily","work"],"japanese":"中止になる、運休する","example_de":"Der Zug fällt heute aus.","example_ja":"その列車は今日運休です。","grammar":{"third_person":"fällt aus","past_participle":"ausgefallen","auxiliary":"sein","separable":true,"reflexive":false,"government":"自動詞"},"collocations":["ein Termin fällt aus","wegen Krankheit ausfallen"],"learning_note":"予定・交通・授業が中止になるときに使う自動詞です。完了形は sein。","related_terms":["absagen","stattfinden"],"source_note":"J-Connect original example and explanation","source_refs":["j-connect-editorial"],"quality_tier":"editorial-reviewed","verification_status":"j-connect-editorial-reviewed","updated_at":"2026-08-14","verified_at":"2026-08-14"},{"card_id":"a2-007","lemma":"umtauschen","display_de":"umtauschen","unit_type":"word","part_of_speech":"verb","primary_level":"A2","level_tags":["A2"],"topic_tags":["shopping","買い物"],"scene_tags":["shopping"],"japanese":"交換する","example_de":"Kann ich den Pullover gegen eine andere Größe umtauschen?","example_ja":"このセーターを別のサイズに交換できますか。","grammar":{"third_person":"tauscht um","past_participle":"umgetauscht","auxiliary":"haben","separable":true,"reflexive":false,"government":"Akkusativ; gegen + Akkusativ"},"collocations":["Ware umtauschen","gegen etwas umtauschen"],"learning_note":"返品して返金を受ける zurückgeben と、品物を交換する umtauschen を区別します。","related_terms":["zurückgeben","reklamieren"],"source_note":"J-Connect original example and explanation","source_refs":["j-connect-editorial"],"quality_tier":"editorial-reviewed","verification_status":"j-connect-editorial-reviewed","updated_at":"2026-08-14","verified_at":"2026-08-14"},{"card_id":"a2-010","lemma":"Sonderangebot","display_de":"das Sonderangebot","unit_type":"word","part_of_speech":"noun","primary_level":"A2","level_tags":["A2"],"topic_tags":["shopping","買い物"],"scene_tags":["shopping"],"japanese":"特売品、特別価格","example_